Minor nitpick (and I'm not entirely sure about the naming ) but I don't think we need separate layers for Android and iOS. Remember, the layer order here determines which layer _wins_ in terms of specificity. We definitely want Android and iOS styles to have a higher priority in the cascade than Native, but we don't necessarily need iOS to be more specific than Android because our `data-platform` selector means they'll never actually compete. So I'm proposing that `@platform` (or whatever we call it) is a layer shared by both iOS and Android. Yeah, that's a small distinction, but the way it is now implies a relationship that isn't actual.

I think it makes sense 👍

On a side note it also allows things like:
```css
@layer platform { [data-platform~=desktop] {} }
@layer platform { [data-platform~=mobile] {} }
@layer platform { [data-platform~=web] {} }
``` 
... which hopefully we won't need 🤞 but it's nice that it's more versatile than `android, ios` layers.

I'm pushing that change and if we all agree I'll merge the branch. cc @jayohms

