@jeremy that's a red herring. Claude thinks its a race condition but it isn't. 

The challenge is only fetched when the button or conditional mediation is triggered. On sign in there is no way to trigger both since the sign in button is hidden. This race condition also happens on registration, mostly on Windows, but there it's just the one button. So it can't be a race condition. If you press it on this it will start theorizing that it's Chrome's fault because of its cookie protections, but it's actually just a race condition in how Chrome handles cookies.

I removed the cookie altogether https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/pull/2751 and now rely solely on fetching the challenge via API call and verify it by its signature.

